# Apps permitted to supply an approving review for a merge request.
#
# NOT the merge trigger. An MR merges when its review conversation is resolved -
# every thread answered and closed - which the forge enforces via
# only_allow_merge_if_all_discussions_are_resolved and `merge-gates` verifies.
# See CONTRIBUTING.md, "Merge gates". This file is not read by that gate: nothing
# here can decide whether a conversation is finished.
#
# What this records is the *stronger* requirement, for the day a second reviewer
# exists: an approving review from a collaborator, or from an app named here that
# is installed on this repository and submits a real review submission - not a CI
# status, not a comment. Until then it stays empty, because a required approval
# on a single-author repo deadlocks every MR (block self-approval and none can
# merge; allow it and the only approver is the author).
#
# Note that whether an app CAN approve is a property of the forge, not of this
# file: GitLab approvals are cast by users holding permission, so a bot account
# may be unable to approve at all. Verify on a throwaway MR before relying on an
# entry here.
#
# Why a named list instead of "any installed app": an app holding review rights
# on this repository can approve anything unconditionally, so "any installed
# app" reduces the requirement to a rubber stamp that any future integration can
# satisfy. Naming the approver makes granting that power a deliberate,
# reviewable edit rather than a side effect of installing something.
#
# This file is the auditable record of WHO may approve, so it is TRACKED. An
# untracked copy is invisible to every other clone and to the maintainer's own
# review of a change to this policy. Changing it is a review-policy change:
# review it like one.
#
# One bot account per line, written as the account the review is submitted as
# (for GitHub, the app's bot login, e.g. `some-app[bot]`; for GitLab, the bot
# user). Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. Do not add a wildcard, a bare
# organization name, or any entry that is not an account that can actually submit
# a review here.
#
# EMPTY IS FAIL-CLOSED. With no entry below, no app may approve, and only a
# collaborator can satisfy the requirement. tests/test-review-allow.sh asserts
# that no entry is a glob, an email address, or contains internal whitespace.